      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the relationship between the measure of an angle and its complement. The complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the original angle, equals 90 degrees. If the measure of the angle is \\( x \\) degrees, then the measure of its complement is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees.\n\nAccording to the problem, the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. This can be expressed with the following equation:\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nNow, let's solve this equation step by step.\n\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\n2. Add \\( 2x \\) to both sides to get all the \\( x \\) terms on one side:\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{60} \\]",
